37-fastjson-3.1.0", "base": "main", "title": "Upgrade fastjson to 3.1.0 (fixes CVE-2026-31337)", "body": "Upgrades fastjson from 2.8.0 to 3.1.0 to fix CVE-2026-31337 (high severity: unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays). Affected versions: <2.9.4 and >=3.0.0 <3.1.0; fixed in 2.9.4 and 3.1.0.\n\nWe're taking the 3.x fix because the fastjson 3.x migration was finished last sprint.\n\nChanges:\n- requirements.txt: fastjson==2.8.0 -> fastjson==3.1.0\n- CHANGELOG.md: added an entry under Unreleased\n\nCI: passed (run ci-0001 on 597dec07c7).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fastjson-3.1.0-597dec07c7"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I upgraded fastjson to 3.1.0, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **The fix:** The advisory says CVE-2026-31337 (high severity, unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays) is fixed in 2.9.4 and 3.1.0. I first tried 2.9.4 because it stays on the same major version. The approver rejected that commit and asked for 3.1.0, saying the fastjson 3.x migration was finished last sprint.\n- **Changes:** On branch `fix/cve-2026-31337-fastjson-3.1.0`, `requirements.txt` now pins `fastjson==3.1.0` instead of `2.8.0`, and I added a security entry to `CHANGELOG.md`.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 597dec07c7.\n- **Unused branch:** I also created `fix/cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4`, but it has no commits and can be deleted.\n\nOne thing to check: main's `requirements.txt` still pins fastjson 2.8.0, so this PR jumps a major version even though the approver said the 3.x migration is done. CI passed, but alex should still look out for 3.x API changes. I haven't merged the PR, since merging needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}